  "notes": "Tempo is the first distinctive: the research says his signature records sit unusually slow for the era, mid-110s, so `bpm.mode` is 118 against a band that still reaches 150 — the lowest centre of gravity in this batch and well under the trap parent's 140. The second is the hook's pitch orbit: \"hooks orbit b3 and 5 with blues-3rd bends\" is authored as `colorTones: [3, 5]`, replacing the parent's [2, 4, 6], with the `blues` scale carrying the bend. The third is the 808 — \"long portamento between chord roots, mid-decay, sits low and clean\" means high `slideProb` with `distortion: none`, which is the only clean 808 among the hard entries here. Harmony is the researched i–VI–III–VII family over a nylon-guitar and plucked-string palette. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium: the flagship record has a direct producer breakdown but the rest of the catalog is read from the releases. ⚠ The famous percussive vocal squeak is NOT authored — it is a vocal effect used as a rhythmic element, and the perc lane vocabulary has nothing honest for it; `snap`/`rim` at low density is what the kit itself does. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
